[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186096742 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" "question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/id #uuid "3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342926" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}(0)$ when $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}.$\n\n${y}^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2)}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡v,\\,v=5x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡v\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡v\\operatorname{cot}⁡v)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+2))\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5(0)+2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5(0)+2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4" :answer/id #uuid "b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\cot(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/id #uuid "72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/math-academy-id "q-28634" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{e}^{x}}\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x}))\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/id #uuid "10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64" "answer-16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b" "answer-3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13" "answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" "answer-a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64" :answer/id #uuid "e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b" :answer/id #uuid "16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13" :answer/id #uuid "3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" :answer/id #uuid "eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea" :answer/id #uuid "a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096845 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" "question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" "question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/id #uuid "6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-31359" :question/problem "Find the slope of $f(x)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nThis question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{4}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{3},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{3})(\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1))+({x}^{4})(-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)-3{x}^{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)(4-3x\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x})|}_{x=1} & =(1)^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3(1)-1)(4-3(1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3(1)-1)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡2(4-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0" "answer-01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4" "answer-b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07" "answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" "answer-638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0" :answer/id #uuid "771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{csc}^{2}⁡2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4" :answer/id #uuid "01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{csc}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07" :answer/id #uuid "b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡2(4+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" :answer/id #uuid "f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡2(4-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039" :answer/id #uuid "638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡3(4-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡3\\operatorname{cot}⁡3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/id #uuid "daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-313291" :question/problem "If $y=2{x}^{4}(5x+3)^{2},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}$(5x+2)(5x+3)$" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=2{x}^{4}$ and $v(x)=(5x+3)^{2}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=8{x}^{3},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=10(5x+3).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(8{x}^{3})(5x+3)^{2}+(2{x}^{4})(10(5x+3)) \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}(5x+3)^{2}+20{x}^{4}(5x+3) \\\\  & =[8(5x+3)+20x]{x}^{3}(5x+3) \\\\  & =[60x+24]{x}^{3}(5x+3) \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}(5x+2)(5x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687" :answer/id #uuid "4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12x^3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/id #uuid "661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11938" :question/problem "Given that $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=1,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))+(x)(\\frac{1}{x+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{x}{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74" "answer-0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e" "answer-47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" "answer-c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141" "answer-27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74" :answer/id #uuid "45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e" :answer/id #uuid "0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" :answer/id #uuid "47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141" :answer/id #uuid "c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800" :answer/id #uuid "27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096893 :activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097788 :step/math-academy-id 635357 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097627 :step/math-academy-id 635358 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097790 :step/math-academy-id 635361 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097789 :step/math-academy-id 635364 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/id #uuid "3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c"] ["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342926"] ["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}(0)$ when $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}.$\n\n${y}^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2)}$"] ["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡v,\\,v=5x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡v\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡v\\operatorname{cot}⁡v)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+2))\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5(0)+2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5(0)+2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e"] ["answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4" :answer/id #uuid "b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4"] ["answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4" :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\cot(2)"] ["answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/correct "answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4"] ["answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e" :answer-field/choices "answer-b80af94b-4a38-5b39-ae68-8d2b740436f4"] ["question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4fe692cc-8ed8-59ce-b082-e2ed1f51f49e"] [17592186096742 :knowledge-point/questions "question-3d0d57c7-6177-5f24-9cc2-07a37c888b6c"] ["question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/id #uuid "72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576"] ["question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/math-academy-id "q-28634"] ["question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})).$"] ["question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{e}^{x}}\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x}))\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/id #uuid "10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847"] ["answer-e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64" :answer/id #uuid "e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64"] ["answer-e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64" :answer/value "2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{x})"] ["answer-16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b" :answer/id #uuid "16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b"] ["answer-16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b" :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})}"] ["answer-3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13" :answer/id #uuid "3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13"] ["answer-3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13" :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})}"] ["answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" :answer/id #uuid "eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190"] ["answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190" :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{x})"] ["answer-a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea" :answer/id #uuid "a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea"] ["answer-a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea" :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({e}^{x})"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/correct "answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/choices "answer-e8d36ad2-0131-5ee0-bd32-9d0f65567d64"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/choices "answer-16cd8e6a-ae7e-5c28-99dd-9074d7853d5b"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/choices "answer-3fee36e7-4401-5e03-9a6b-6965838f4a13"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/choices "answer-eae569df-63de-52d0-bf54-e46020840190"] ["answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847" :answer-field/choices "answer-a70eed8e-5be1-5524-9a26-66c8b46cc3ea"] ["question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-10155cd6-2910-5836-92ab-09e1570ab847"] [17592186096742 :knowledge-point/questions "question-72dac6dc-e0ce-50af-9f12-1cecf652f576"] ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/id #uuid "6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7"] ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-31359"] ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/problem "Find the slope of $f(x)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)$ at $x=1.$"] ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nThis question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{4}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{3},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{3})(\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1))+({x}^{4})(-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)-3{x}^{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3x-1)(4-3x\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x})|}_{x=1} & =(1)^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3(1)-1)(4-3(1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3(1)-1)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡2(4-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b"] ["answer-771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0" :answer/id #uuid "771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0"] ["answer-771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0" :answer/value "-3{csc}^{2}⁡2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2)"] ["answer-01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4" :answer/id #uuid "01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4"] ["answer-01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4" :answer/value "4\\operatorname{csc}⁡2"] ["answer-b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07" :answer/id #uuid "b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07"] ["answer-b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07" :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡2(4+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2)"] ["answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" :answer/id #uuid "f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a"] ["answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a" :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡2(4-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡2)"] ["answer-638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039" :answer/id #uuid "638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039"] ["answer-638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039" :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡3(4-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡3\\operatorname{cot}⁡3)"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/correct "answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/choices "answer-771e64c9-e943-52fe-945f-1eea480889b0"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/choices "answer-01c722ff-e1b8-5a52-af6d-46d7d47770f4"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/choices "answer-b5d1c180-4dd3-51bf-b383-ca38bfcc7a07"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/choices "answer-f2c9181f-174f-587d-914d-0780f3a3d35a"] ["answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b" :answer-field/choices "answer-638ce517-cf18-5e4a-9cb3-d4f7d60d0039"] ["question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c3ecdc8b-e818-5576-b257-904854acad1b"] [17592186096845 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6650c0b4-dbaf-54fa-bdff-16ce8ac264e7"] ["question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/id #uuid "daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f"] ["question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-313291"] ["question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/problem "If $y=2{x}^{4}(5x+3)^{2},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}$(5x+2)(5x+3)$"] ["question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=2{x}^{4}$ and $v(x)=(5x+3)^{2}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=8{x}^{3},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=10(5x+3).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(8{x}^{3})(5x+3)^{2}+(2{x}^{4})(10(5x+3)) \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}(5x+3)^{2}+20{x}^{4}(5x+3) \\\\  & =[8(5x+3)+20x]{x}^{3}(5x+3) \\\\  & =[60x+24]{x}^{3}(5x+3) \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}(5x+2)(5x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d"] ["answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687" :answer/id #uuid "4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687"] ["answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687" :answer/value "12x^3"] ["answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/correct "answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687"] ["answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d" :answer-field/choices "answer-4d00388d-a12d-56fd-8d51-d495691cc687"] ["question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-8b851d6d-50e9-5279-a1fc-f460b437e85d"] [17592186096845 :knowledge-point/questions "question-daf70261-77b1-5e20-8f5a-cedbd73a4a6f"] ["question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/id #uuid "661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7"] ["question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11938"] ["question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/problem "Given that $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$"] ["question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=1,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))+(x)(\\frac{1}{x+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{x}{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-661f8f17-e856-564e-ad3f-b602958b65c7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f"] ["answer-45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74" :answer/id #uuid "45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74"] ["answer-45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-45b25f33-bf7f-5def-955e-d497d26f5e74" :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+(x+1)"] ["answer-0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e" :answer/id #uuid "0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e"] ["answer-0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0938a141-d12b-51e1-9998-a7cc436edc0e" :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{1}{x+1}"] ["answer-47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" :answer/id #uuid "47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770"] ["answer-47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-47dee097-bdf3-5c60-8d1d-d16d58555770" :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{x}{x+1}"] ["answer-c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141" :answer/id #uuid "c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141"] ["answer-c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c9028022-51bc-53f4-aee2-72790be92141" :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{1}{x+1}"] ["answer-27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800" :answer/id #uuid "27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800"] ["answer-27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-27fa3f4c-12dc-5dbf-874a-1e6639271800" :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\frac{x}{x+1}"] ["answer-field-0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0ef58acd-fd9a-5753-af67-91bee6f1e34f" :answer